Go ahead, Bear.

263
00:24:10,060 --> 00:24:11,589
What were you just saying?

264
00:24:11,840 --> 00:24:12,670
So,

265
00:24:12,753 --> 00:24:14,817
tomorrow morning at around 1 a .m.,

266
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:18,017
Straw Hat's ship should be
showing up at Cacao Island,

267
00:24:18,100 --> 00:24:21,688
assuming we don't manage to kill
them before then, of course.

268
00:24:22,040 --> 00:24:22,870
Here?

269
00:24:22,953 --> 00:24:24,360
At 1 a .m.?

270
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:33,357
The plan was to meet up with the Sunny
at sea and hand over the wedding cake.

271
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:34,270
What happened?

272
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:41,776
Why would the Straw Hats
want to come to Kaku Island?

273
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:42,800
It's simple.

274
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:46,437
That's where they were planning
to meet up with their captain,

275
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:51,167
who split up on the rest of the group,
thinking that he could help them escape.

276
00:24:54,440 --> 00:24:55,270
I see.

277
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:57,437
But if the enemy knows their plan,

278
00:24:57,520 --> 00:25:00,057
this island's going to be
crawling with their soldiers.

279
00:25:00,140 --> 00:25:01,300
The thing is...

280
00:25:03,980 --> 00:25:08,740
Even if they do make it to Kaku Island,
Straw Hat Luffy certainly will not.

281
00:25:09,660 --> 00:25:11,072
And what does that mean?

282
00:25:11,540 --> 00:25:12,900
That he won't be alive.

283
00:25:13,240 --> 00:25:18,122
The idiot pushed his luck and challenged
Big Brother Katakuri to a one-on-one duel.

284
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:31,680
So you can imagine how
well that's working out.

285
00:25:31,920 --> 00:25:33,680
It serves him right, I say.

286
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:40,500
All right, heave home!

287
00:25:43,240 --> 00:25:45,020
It's four o 'clock now.

288
00:25:46,580 --> 00:25:49,077
That means in about nine hours,

289
00:25:49,160 --> 00:25:52,317
the Straw Hats will arrive
at Kaku Island and wait

290
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:55,360
for their precious captain
who will never appear.

291
00:25:56,700 --> 00:26:01,582
Mama still suffering from hunger pangs and
Press will show up around the same time.

292
00:26:02,080 --> 00:26:04,786
Everyone will be gathered
to see the big show.

293
00:26:05,220 --> 00:26:08,632
Needless to say, we can't
afford for anything to go wrong.

294
00:26:09,120 --> 00:26:12,120
We're counting on you to
take care of Mama Pudding.

295
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:14,140
You're our only hope.

296
00:26:15,020 --> 00:26:16,940
Don't worry, sis. I've got this.

297
00:26:17,260 --> 00:26:21,613
If Mama wants the greatest wedding
cake ever, then that's what she'll get.

298
00:26:23,960 --> 00:26:25,800
I'll look forward to it then.

299
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:32,240
Oh, by the way, if the Straw Hats happen
to arrive ahead of time, don't worry.

300
00:26:34,100 --> 00:26:36,218
Oven just showed up with his troops.

301
00:26:36,520 --> 00:26:39,060
They'll take care of things for you. What?

302
00:26:39,380 --> 00:26:41,556
Did you say that Oven's here already?

303
00:26:50,580 --> 00:26:53,992
What do you mean I can't enter
the damn factory right now?

304
00:26:54,660 --> 00:26:57,307
That's, uh, Lake Pudding's
order, I'm afraid.

305
00:26:57,440 --> 00:26:58,420
I'm her brother.

306
00:26:59,020 --> 00:26:59,902
I'm sorry, sir.

307
00:27:00,280 --> 00:27:03,597
Well, if she's that insistent,
then I will honor the request.

308
00:27:03,680 --> 00:27:07,680
But if the factory is supposed to
be off limits, then why the crowd?

309
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:09,960
Oh, uh, yes, it's about that.

310
00:27:10,600 --> 00:27:11,430
Hey!

311
00:27:12,820 --> 00:27:13,737
Come on!

312
00:27:13,820 --> 00:27:15,760
So it's you.

313
00:27:25,980 --> 00:27:27,860
Why are you hurting me?

314
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:28,980
I'm no threat.

315
00:27:29,220 --> 00:27:30,985
Because you're a damn stalker.

316
00:27:31,360 --> 00:27:33,140
How could you say that?

317
00:27:33,340 --> 00:27:35,100
Don't you remember me, Oven?

318
00:27:36,380 --> 00:27:38,140
Of course I remember you.

319
00:27:38,360 --> 00:27:40,080
You used to be my stepfather.

320
00:27:40,620 --> 00:27:42,444
I'm glad you haven't forgotten.

321
00:27:42,820 --> 00:27:45,020
I know it's been a long time now.

322
00:27:45,340 --> 00:27:50,164
But if you understand my situation, then
maybe you could stop punching me, please.

323
00:27:53,460 --> 00:27:55,931
I'm afraid that you've got this backwards.

324
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:57,070
Huh?

325
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:00,180
It's a lot of noise.

326
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:01,929
I hope it's not a problem.

327
00:28:02,100 --> 00:28:03,159
He just got a pig.

328
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:06,760
Sanji, are you listening? To your call?

329
00:28:07,020 --> 00:28:08,577
Your captain's in big trouble.

330
00:28:08,660 --> 00:28:10,060
Eh, he'll be fine.

331
00:28:10,380 --> 00:28:11,420
What do you mean?

332
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:14,739
Challenging Katakuri to a
duel is insanely reckless.

333
00:28:15,240 --> 00:28:16,380
Sounds like Luffy.

334
00:28:17,100 --> 00:28:19,197
Katakuri's bounty is over a billion.

335
00:28:19,280 --> 00:28:21,633
His strength's superhuman next to Luffy.

336
00:28:21,980 --> 00:28:25,640
Big Brother has never lost a
single fight in his entire life.

337
00:28:26,160 --> 00:28:27,866
Then it's a special occasion.

338
00:28:29,260 --> 00:28:31,540
He's about to lose for the first time.

339
00:28:32,380 --> 00:28:34,280
We just need to do our part.

340
00:28:34,540 --> 00:28:37,422
And that's making the
greatest wedding cake ever.

341
00:28:40,980 --> 00:28:42,980
Your captain is as good as dead.

342
00:28:43,320 --> 00:28:45,360
No one has ever defeated Katakuri,

343
00:28:45,480 --> 00:28:48,757
and he's not about to lose to some
lame-ass pirate crew like yours.

344
00:28:48,840 --> 00:28:49,980
Cue that, Sanji.

345
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:52,240
Relax, Pudding.

346
00:28:53,260 --> 00:28:54,860
Just focus on work.

347
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:56,240
We've got this.

348
00:28:56,860 --> 00:28:58,020
Let's have fun.

349
00:28:58,340 --> 00:29:00,752
I'm glad we get to do a project together.

350
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:06,870
Sanji!

351
00:29:08,660 --> 00:29:09,697
Does she have a fever?

352
00:29:09,780 --> 00:29:11,057
Maybe someone baked her?

353
00:29:11,140 --> 00:29:11,970
Not likely!

354
00:29:14,600 --> 00:29:15,720
Lady Pony!

355
00:29:21,600 --> 00:29:23,640
Guess nobody's coming after us.

356
00:29:24,180 --> 00:29:25,760
Something must be amiss.

357
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:29,494
They'd surely send pursuers
by now if they were able to.

358
00:29:29,580 --> 00:29:31,357
You think something happened then?

359
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:33,080
I wonder if this is a trap.

360
00:29:33,380 --> 00:29:34,440
Don't worry, Nami.

361
00:29:34,680 --> 00:29:38,268
I promise that we won't let our
guard down even for a second.

362
00:29:39,380 --> 00:29:40,680
That reminds me.

363
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:43,901
I hope Aladdin and the
others escaped here safely.

364
00:29:44,300 --> 00:29:47,182
Perhaps they were able to
slip away in the chaos.

365
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:48,560
What did you say?

366
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:52,517
Briss, I thought Mama was
supposed to be chasing Straw Hats.

367
00:29:52,600 --> 00:29:54,482
Why is she wrecking Nuts Island?

368
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:56,420
It's not my fault.

369
00:29:56,560 --> 00:29:57,720
Excuse me, Mandor.

370
00:29:57,900 --> 00:29:59,160
I have bad news.

371
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:01,120
Oh, bad news, you say?

372
00:30:01,360 --> 00:30:03,457
Don't have enough of that, now do we?

373
00:30:03,540 --> 00:30:05,658
We scanned all of the waters nearby.

374
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:08,160
We searched for the slugs, but...

375
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:11,980
The thing is...

376
00:30:13,220 --> 00:30:14,050
WHAT?!

377
00:30:14,133 --> 00:30:18,097
What do you mean that all of
the territory slugs are gone?!

378
00:30:18,180 --> 00:30:19,298
Where did they go?!

379
00:30:19,780 --> 00:30:21,717
You don't suppose they're dead, do you?

380
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:23,565
There's not a single one left!

381
00:30:24,900 --> 00:30:26,665
But there's thousands of them!

382
00:30:26,800 --> 00:30:30,094
They can't all disappear at
once without a single trace!

383
00:30:30,340 --> 00:30:32,260
Maybe someone kidnapped them?

384
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:34,266
How would they pull that off?

385
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:37,157
Anyway, we can't have enemy
ships running wild out there!

386
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:38,960
Go and fix this now!

387
00:30:39,260 --> 00:30:41,720
Um, I can try, but how?

388
00:30:42,120 --> 00:30:44,620
Just find out why they're gone, you idiot!

389
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:46,900
Get moving! Yasuie, sir!

390
00:31:02,940 --> 00:31:07,537
Sea slugs, why don't you sing with me?

391
00:31:07,620 --> 00:31:10,937
Everyone, be carefree.

392
00:31:11,020 --> 00:31:14,237
Take the day off.

393
00:31:14,320 --> 00:31:16,397
You've worked hard enough.

394
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:20,160
We'll all have fun, you'll see.

395
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:23,720
Security, let it be.

396
00:31:24,280 --> 00:31:28,280
Transmitting, now is the time to play.

397
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:30,280
All day!

398
00:31:38,580 --> 00:31:42,640
Now doesn't this feel so heavenly?

399
00:31:47,540 --> 00:31:53,360
So you see, it's better to be lazy.
